  {
    "chunk_id": "chunk_5",
    "source": "recommendation_rules.md",
    "title": "2. Recommendation Strategies",
    "text": "Document: recommendation_rules.md\nSection: 2. Recommendation Strategies\n### A. Stock-Out Risk & Low Stock Action Guidelines\n- **Predictive Stock-Out Risk / Low Stock**:\n  - Issue expedited purchase reorder to supplier.\n  - Evaluate store-to-store inventory rebalancing from nearby stores with surplus stock.\n  - Temporarily pause marketing promotions on low-stock items until replenishment arrives.\n\n### B. Overstocked & Slow-Moving Action Guidelines\n- **Overstock / Slow-Moving Products**:\n  - Implement promotional discount or bundle offer with complementary high-demand products.\n  - Adjust future reorder parameters and lower target stock levels.\n  - Review end-cap product placement or store merchandising to increase visibility.\n\n### C. Sales Spike Action Guidelines\n- **Surging Demand / Sales Spike**:\n  - Verify safety stock levels and prepare advance replenishment orders.\n  - Ensure shelf space allocation matches elevated sales velocity.\n\n### D. Sales Drop Action Guidelines\n- **Demand Collapse / Sales Drop**:\n  - Investigate product display, stock availability, or price positioning.\n  - Check for localized store issues or shifting consumer demand patterns.",
